 - Only managers may delete tasks.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
+- Moving a task (`/move`) needs the same edit right as updating it in the
+  source project (managers any task, contributors only their own; a denial
+  is 403 and is checked before the target is looked up). The target project
+  must be readable by the user (else 404), must have a contributor or manager
+  role for the user (else 403), and must not be archived (409). Moving a task
+  to the project it is already in → 400.
+- A move keeps the task's ID, title, status and assignee. The assignee must be
+  a contributor or manager of the target project, otherwise the move is 400 and
+  nothing changes.
 
